WEBVTT

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:02.950
Chihaya...

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.060
Chihaya...

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.340
Chihaya...

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.100
Eek! What is this?!

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.170
<i>Is this the magic of smartphones?!</i>

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:20.700
<b>It's a late-night show, 
but I'm a regular in it</b>

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.380
<i>Don't miss the next episode of
<i>Smartphone Magic: XL Love!</i></i>

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.290
What... kind of role is this, Chitose?

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.630
I'm playing the friend of a high school girl
who gets a phone app that makes people fat!

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.900
You won't have that "fat" makeup 
in every episode, will you?

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.460
Chihaya...

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.460
Chihaya...

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.440
I love you.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:41.140
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.970
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
<b>Final Exams
Study Week</b>

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.010
Verse 15

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.010
As helpless 
autumn
 leaves
 are caught 
against
 the flow

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:00.950
<i>I love you.</i>

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.260
Hey, Chihaya...

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.840
Why have you had that shocked look 
on your face all this time?

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.050
P-Pres—

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:08.630
Oe-senpai!

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:10.630
Come with me a sec!
I have a literature question!

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.020
She's sure enthusiastic.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.140
Oe-senpai, what were you 
going to tell him?!

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.150
N-Nothing, honest.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.830
I wouldn't talk about that stuff
in the club room.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.750
You're not going to tell him, are you?

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.900
That Wataya-san confessed 
his love to Ayase-senpai?

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.400
No one except the people involved 
has any right to butt in.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.590
But...

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.030
If President Mashima could become involved...

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.540
I might say something.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:45.590
Don't!

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:47.700
It's something Ayase-senpai 
has to think about!

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.300
If you tell Mashima-senpai,
it'll put incredible pressure on him!

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.550
Just let them be!

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.070
Y-You're just saying that

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:58.230
because it'd be convenient for you
if Chihaya-chan dated someone else.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.020
That is part of it!

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:03.070
But that was a hurdle Mashima-senpai 
couldn't get over,

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:09.040
<b>Soar</b>

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.910
and Wataya-san cleared it with ease!

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.770
Don't you think they'd be perfect
 for each other?

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.080
Well—

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.220
Yes, they would!

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.140
And outsiders shouldn't interfere!

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.370
Let's just watch over them! Okay?!

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.510
If you want...

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.380
let's play karuta together.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.040
<i>Wataya-san is really something.</i>

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.050
<i>To people who take karuta 
as seriously as they do,</i>

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.460
<i>"let's play karuta together" must mean...</i>

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.040
<i>Prez!</i>

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.350
Chihaya... you know, Arata...

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.560
Huh? What, Taichi?

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.740
Uh, nothing.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:51.420
Hey, by the way, Taichi... 
you knew, didn't you?

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:52.650
Huh? Knew what?

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.380
A—

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:55.410
A...

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:59.850
A-Ah... A... A... A...

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:08.220
Ara... Arata... said he wants 
to go to college here...

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:13.940
Ayase!

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.310
If you're not going to study, just leave.
You're distracting me.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.440
<b>Rustle Rustle</b>

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.910
S-S-Sorry, Desktomu-kun!

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:20.190
I'm gonna get a drink of water!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.190
<b>Zoom</b>

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.450
<i>Maybe the rest of them have forgotten,</i>

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:26.120
<i>but I'm still aiming for 
the top of our grade!</i>

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.580
<b>Always top of the national
science curriculum</b>

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.590
<i>I'll take down Mashima Taichi!</i>

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:29.940
<i>But...</i>

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:36.420
<b>1st in grade</b>

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:36.420
<b>2nd</b>

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:43.470
<b>Whoosh</b>

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.180
<i>Since Mashima's striving for the 
pinnacle of the karuta world,</i>

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.440
<i>being top of our grade 
is a matter of course.</i>

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:41.030
<i>What keeps Mashima going is the pressure of 
having to quit karuta if his grades drop.</i>

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:43.470
The stage for strong
 karuta players

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:43.470
<b>Oh ho ho ho!</b>

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.470
It's all right if you fall, you know!

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.460
<i>I don't have that urgency pushing me.</i>

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:46.310
I'm back. Oe-senpai's in the bathroom.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:47.960
<i>If I do make it to the top of our grade...</i>

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:50.350
<i>maybe I'll tell Kana-chan...</i>

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.950
<i>that I like her.</i>

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.230
<b>Ah!</b>

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.740
<i>But it's wrong to treat Kana-chan 
as bait to get me to the top!</i>

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.230
<b>Ah!</b>

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.070
<i>Also, that is way too lenient!</i>

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.400
<i>I'd have to make it so I can "never, ever" 
tell her that if I don't come in first!</i>

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.820
<b>Ah!</b>

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.400
<i>Never, ever?! I don't think I want that...</i>

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.150
Argh!

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.350
Let's think about something fun instead!

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.740
What should we do for Christmas?

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.160
It's not like any of us have 
boyfriends or girlfriends, right?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.420
So let's do something together!

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.030
<i>Darn it, Porky-senpai!</i>

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.960
<i>That's a live landmine you're stepping on!</i>

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.110
Couldn't we hang out at 
your house, Mashima?

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.020
Uh, I don't think so.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.790
What's wrong with you, Tsukuba?!

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:34.300
My little brothers are saying they 
want to meet Santa Claus...

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:38.440
February 
Bean-throwing 
Festival

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:39.560
<b>I even wore a muscle suit...</b>

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.970
Hey, Bro! I don't think 
that ogre's an ogre!

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.550
Those are the socks Dad was wearing!

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:44.610
My family... We can't keep their dreams
alive by ourselves anymore...

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.610
<i>That couldn't possibly 
matter less right now!</i>

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.240
Is something out there?

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.300
Yeah. That pigeon.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:01.060
Oh, I see it. It's a white one.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.130
Those are rare.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.890
It's pretty.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.830
It almost seems like it's shining.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.520
I wonder... is it pregnant?

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:13.110
Is it happy?

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.610
Is it shining because it's happy?

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:27.740
<i>Fujiwara no Atsutada 
The emotions experienced after a long-awaited reunion banish any lingering memories of the past</i>

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.420
Mom, does this poem mean

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:24.530
that after a tryst, the author realized that
he'd been completely naïve in the past?

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.100
That's right.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:25.860
<b>What a 
question for a 
seven-year-old...</b>

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.110
<b>Age 7</b>

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:29.990
But I think there's a much 
more special meaning to it.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.990
<b>A "tryst," she says...</b>

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:35.510
When my gynecologist told 
me I was pregnant,

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.120
With you, of course

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:37.370
I felt like that, too.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.690
Huh? Really?

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:39.900
What I mean is...

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:44.140
There are moments when you 
learn something so life-altering

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.980
that it turns you into a different person.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.400
On my way home from the hospital that day,

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.590
the world I saw was shining bright,
and so, so beautiful.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:57.800
And I thought, "I'm not who 
I used to be anymore."

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.720
"A new chapter has just begun."

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.500
Kana-chan...

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.150
I want...

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.780
to play a match like that one 
at the challenger playoffs.

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:23.450
<i>Huh?! Chihaya-chan, I think
you're conflating something here!</i>

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:27.800
<i>You're mixing up your emotional response to
Dr. Harada's play and Wataya-san's confession!</i>

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.640
<i>I know they were both 
epoch-making events, but...</i>

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.470
<b>Bye-bye

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:34.480
<i>As a young girl, shouldn't the 
confession be your main focus?!</i>

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:37.890
Chihaya-chan!

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.570
Man, the leaves are really falling.

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:42.640
It's even been said 
that newly fallen autumn leaves

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:45.820
are such a vivid red that they might 
be emitting their own light.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.290
<i>They're so pretty.</i>

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.650
<i>I don't even want to step on them.</i>

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.650
<i>That was a hurdle Mashima-senpai 
couldn't get over,</i>

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:00.670
<i>and Wataya-san cleared it with ease!</i>

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:03.670
<i>Don't you think they'd be 
perfect for each other?</i>

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:09.940
<i>I'm hoping that things work out
between Ayase-senpai and Wataya-san.</i>

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.500
<i>If she rejects Mashima-senpai,</i>

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.780
<i>I actually believe he'd 
be mine for the taking.</i>

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:18.370
<i>I would rather choose the 
girl I devote myself to.</i>

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:20.680
<i>I'm going to beat Chihaya.</i>

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:25.110
<i>I'm wishing for someone 
who's trying so hard</i>

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:27.900
<i>to have his heart crushed to bits.</i>

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:32.490
<i>I don't want to step on them,
but I do anyway.</i>

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:35.750
<i>This red so vivid that it seems to burn...</i>

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.990
<i>Mashima-senpai, what are you going to do?</i>

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:43.230
<i>Wataya-san came out and said it!</i>

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:44.850
<i>It's already begun!</i>

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.780
<i>And it might be ending for you!</i>

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.950
Oh, that's mine.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.810
Who's that? I don't know this number.

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.300
It's me, Sudo.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.510
Wh-Wh-Wh-Which Sudo-san might you be?

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:05.300
You didn't save that contact
under my name?

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.850
How do you know my number?

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:10.510
We traded contact info last year, remember?

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:12.320
It's not that I had anything to talk about.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.030
<b><i>I</i> don't...</b>

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:15.320
But someone from my college 
karuta club does.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.660
Well, I only just found out
he was in my club...

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:21.080
This is Suo.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:24.950
Will you play a match with me sometime?

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:28.750
Since you asked me the other day...

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:33.010
<b>Hold the phone closer!</b>

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:32.990
How about a match with me?

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:36.860
A m-match...

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:39.710
with Suo-san...

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.260
With the current Master...

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:43.720
I'll—

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:44.230
We'll do it!

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:53.190
Well, now that final exams are over...

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:57.610
<b>Cough                     Cough</b>

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:57.600
Do you have a clearer idea on
which subject you want to specialize in?

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:01.630
I've...

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:04.880
I've been trying to improve all-around 
so I can choose any of them!

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:04.870
<b>Bang</b>

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.370
<b>Dash</b>

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.380
I'll keep thinking about it!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:10.420
So you can choose any of them?

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.830
I'm not so sure...

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.210
Science and math are out...

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:16.870
Ah, she still shines as much as ever in PE!

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.880
<b>Classical Literature             Japanese History</b>

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.900
And her social studies grades are up.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:23.590
Which doorknob will she choose?

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:28.140
Mr. Fukasaku, what are you 
muttering to yourself about?

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:31.820
Well, you see, I think 
of advancing to college

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:36.190
as the last chance to choose 
a door with a knob.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.150
Huh? Knob?

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.020
It's something I heard long ago.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:44.540
Most doors leading to opportunities 
don't have a knob.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:47.870
You can't open them yourself.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:52.530
It becomes a matter of whether or not 
you can dive in when it's opened to you,

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:57.610
and whether or not
you can seize that opportunity.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.550
<b>Tokyo University</b>

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:03.470
What the heck is this, Taichi?!

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:08.060
<b>I don't know why I'm crying...</b>

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:06.420
I know Sudo-san said last year that
he wanted to go to a national university...

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:08.050
But Tokyo U?!

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:09.300
Not only that...

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:11.500
but Suo-san, too?!

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:15.380
Suo-san's karuta society profile 
doesn't list his university.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.280
<b>Out of consideration to Tokyo U, maybe...</b>

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.040
Suo-san had to repeat a year here four times?!

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:20.420
Is he smart or stupid?!

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.200
<b>From: Sudo Akihito 

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.950
Did you see the Yasuda Auditorium? 
That should make a nice memory. 

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:26.990
<b>We actually practice at Hakusan Hall
in Bunkyo Ward, you idiot.</b>

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.090
Curse you, Double Su!

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:28.810
What's that mean?!

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.940
They're Suo and Sudo, so they're Double Su!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:32.740
Is this it?

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:34.010
Are they in the back?

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:35.260
Hey.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.130
Been a while.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.450
Why'd you two come together?

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:43.890
<b>Chill</b>

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:41.070
Nothing better to do? You dating?

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:42.290
Huh? Huh?

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:42.940
S-Sudo-san...

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:43.880
Hey, it's you.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:45.970
Goo— Kosaku...

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.130
Koishikawa-san?

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.650
Aren't you in KU's karuta club?

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:51.730
Oh, yeah, I am.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.640
But I came back here since it's fall again.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.900
<b>Like fall salmon, kinda?</b>

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:55.890
It's the fall Suo season.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:12:00.900
<b>Fall Suo...</b>

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:58.970
Suo-san only practices for 
about two months each year,

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:01.240
from November up until the Master match.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.160
Huh?!

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:04.910
I mean, he does show up 
at other times, too.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.160
He actually looks out for his club mates,

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.200
so he drops in now and then and
serves snacks instead of practicing.

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.200
Are you in Class A?

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.290
I'm still in Class B.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.280
You get three rice dumplings, then.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:15.410
Keep at it.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:16.200
And you?

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.530
I'm in Class C.

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:18.170
You get two.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.330
Hey, Suo-san, did you hear?

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:24.790
NHK BS isn't going to broadcast
the Master match live this year.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:26.560
I can't believe it.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:31.600
<b>Bubble
Bubble</b>

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:34.300
Oh... But it'll be streamed 
live on Niconico.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.200
Nico?!

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.770
Ow! That's hot!

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:37.830
Wow, that startled me.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.260
Suo-san!

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:40.110
I've never heard Suo-san yell before.

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:42.990
His enthusiasm just visibly dropped, didn't it?

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:47.100
I think the live nationwide broadcast was 
a major source of motivation for him.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.510
<i>Ni... Nico...</i>

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:50.240
<i>Clap, clap, clap, clap, clap...</i>

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.240
Are you in Class A?

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:52.960
Yes!

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:53.740
We're in Class A!

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:55.750
<b>Empty...</b>

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:55.750
<b>Filled to the brim...</b>

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:57.740
Whoa, they're gonna fall out...

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.000
<b>Nothing but beans...</b>

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.000
<b>Nothing but beans...              Gotta eat it fast</b>

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.750
<i>I'm her boyfriend. Please don't 
try anything with her.</i>

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:03.250
<i>I hate him!</i>

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:10.880
Wait, don't tell me...

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:12.900
You don't have a hair tie, Suo-san?

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:14.270
He forgot it?

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:14.930
Anyone have one?

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:16.010
I only have scrunchies.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:23.140
I always thought Suo-san was more 
of a lone wolf that nobody liked,

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:25.770
but it's more like everyone's 
doting on him.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.070
No one wants to play a 
match with him, though.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:37.040
<b>Super persistent type</b>

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:31.650
Partly because he's too good,
but that's not all.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:35.280
Koishikawa-san and I are the only ones 
who ever want to challenge him again.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:37.040
<b>The type that never learns</b>

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.600
There aren't enough Class A 
practice partners for him.

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:39.950
That's probably why he asked for you.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:42.920
Go get turned to mincemeat.

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:55.970
You're too far away.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:56.770
Sorry!

00:13:58.030 --> 00:13:59.530
No hope for her.

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:00.830
You just gonna watch?

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:01.310
Uh...

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:03.010
Come play me!

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:06.470
Koishikawa-san, he says 
he'd rather watch Ayase.

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:09.170
No, let me play you, Sudo-san.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.230
I came to get some practice of my own.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:18.880
<i>This tightness in my chest isn't 
because of those rice dumplings.</i>

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:20.600
<i>But...</i>

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:25.120
<i>it feels like a bunch of them are 
stacked up in my esophagus.</i>

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:27.700
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.970
<i>I can't look up.</i>

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.660
<i>It's hard to breathe... What do I do?</i>

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.180
Chihaya...

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:35.700
I love you.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.640
<b>Blush</b>

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.490
<i>Oh, right! This is the Master!</i>

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:46.140
<i>The one Dr. Harada and Arata wanted 
so badly to play against!</i>

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:58.640
<i>My belly's full, and my body's moving well.</i>

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:02.610
<i>Suo-san, I...</i>

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:06.620
<i>haven't really imagined 
myself playing you before,</i>

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:12.980
<i>but I've tried harder to become you 
in practice than anyone here.</i>

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:20.640
<i>Since the dew atop the blades of grass 
has been scattered by the winds,</i>

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:19.240
<i>He knew exactly where the card was
and held it down,</i>

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:20.640
<i>taking a two-syllable card on the first.</i>

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.270
<i>I've watched him over and over. 
Don't be surprised.</i>

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:30.120
<i>When I must hide...</i>

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.910
<i>It's like magic... It almost 
stops my breathing.</i>

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:35.700
<i>May the time spent...</i>

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.450
<b>Go ahead.</b>

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:40.830
<i>He really isn't going for 
multi-syllable cards.</i>

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:44.150
<i>The hazed early dawn light...</i>

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:46.440
<i>He has his eyes on the match as a whole.</i>

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:49.090
<i>He only needs to get to 25 cards first.</i>

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.900
<i>He has 28 one-syllable cards.</i>

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:55.430
<i>If he just takes all the cards he sees 
as one-syllable cards, he wins.</i>

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.090
<i>How can I throw him off his gameplan?</i>

00:15:58.090 --> 00:15:59.890
<i>Gust of wind leaves...</i>

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.950
<i>Yes!</i>

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.890
<i>My game sense is working!
I heard the first syllable coming!</i>

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.990
<i>But this isn't it.</i>

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:12.560
<i>It's not the actual one-syllable cards
that I should worry about.</i>

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:17.070
<i>Where I really need to break 
Suo-san's pace is...</i>

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:18.650
<i>Feel love deepen...</i>

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.220
<i>Got it!</i>

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:22.190
<i>A two-syllable card on the first syllable!</i>

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:24.920
<i>My weapon, the one Desktomu-kun 
told me about!</i>

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:28.160
<i>I can do this! I can fight him!</i>

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.570
<i>Concentrate.</i>

00:16:38.570 --> 00:16:40.780
<i>If I lose focus, this won't 
even be a match anymore.</i>

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:42.310
<i>Concentrate!</i>

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:45.960
<i>When winds send waves...</i>

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.410
<i>Shoot! A fault!</i>

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:51.240
<i>Concentrate. One more time.</i>

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:54.420
<i>As this trip takes...</i>

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:55.880
<i>Another fault!</i>

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:58.060
<i>But Suo-san cleanly avoided it!</i>

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:02.830
<i>Come to think of it, when Takemura-san
was in the Master match,</i>

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.720
<i>he wasn't out of his league.</i>

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:06.040
<i>He just had a lot of faults.</i>

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.000
<i>Feel sorrow wash...</i>

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.870
<i>When I try not to take the bait,
I move too late!</i>

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:13.400
<i>A semi-double!</i>

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.580
<i>No! Concentrate!</i>

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:16.330
Pff...

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:22.200
<i>Ayase...</i>

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:25.220
<i>Suo-san has no intention 
of taking 25 cards.</i>

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:27.670
<i>He always comes in under 20.</i>

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:30.100
<i>His opponent could take 
30 cards and still lose.</i>

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:33.510
<i>He moves knowing full well
that these are dead cards!</i>

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:37.210
<i>No one else plays karuta
the same nasty way he does.</i>

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:38.920
<i>A trap.</i>

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:40.110
<i>It's not to win.</i>

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:41.180
<i>A trap.</i>

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:42.250
<i>What's it for?</i>

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.270
<i>A trap.</i>

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:50.110
<i>The differentials of 5 and 13 cards are the 
same as in the Queen matches, aren't they?</i>

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:53.120
<i>To take control over karuta itself.</i>

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:55.980
<i>I thought it was a fluke.</i>

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:59.130
<i>If he's aiming to win by 
the same number of cards,</i>

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:01.500
<i>that means there are cards 
he could take, but won't.</i>

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:05.320
<i>He lures his opponent into making 
mistakes to make the numbers match.</i>

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.980
<i>I had no idea anyone played like that...</i>

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:13.050
<i>An honest idiot like Ayase
will just get sucked right in.</i>

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:15.820
<i>He drags his opponents into his pace.</i>

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:18.080
<i>That's why he's the Master.</i>

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:21.410
<i>Whoops... I should be worrying 
about my own game.</i>

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.290
<i>Did he...</i>

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:26.920
<i>always play karuta like this?</i>

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:30.480
<i>He was always able to utilize
all kinds of different techniques,</i>

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:32.930
<i>but he was really a jack of all 
trades and master of none.</i>

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.720
<i>Now he's settled down.</i>

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:39.010
<i>I'm in the place where Sudo-san,
Koishikawa-san, and even Master Suo practice.</i>

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.700
<i>You'd have to be positive 
to last in here.</i>

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:42.760
<i>Especially...</i>

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:44.750
<i>Koishikawa-san.</i>

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.520
<b>D'oh</b>

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.350
<b>He goofed again 

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:47.980
<b>Flip</b>

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:48.390
<i>But that's who I am!</i>

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.390
<b>He bounced back 

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.270
<i>Including all my goof-ups!</i>

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.620
<i>I want to be like that.</i>

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:54.530
<i>And that's...</i>

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.410
<i>something I can never be.</i>

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:00.090
<i>Keep my hands lower.</i>

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:01.870
<i>I can get underneath to take 
multi-syllable cards.</i>

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.520
<i>Take a position where it's 
easy to make a pull-back.</i>

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:05.450
<i>Check the "My" and "No" cards.</i>

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.000
<i>I'll lose if I rush on "I," 
"So," and "Would" cards, too.</i>

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.720
Taichi... you knew, didn't you?

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.100
<i>Guard...</i>

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:12.790
Arata said he wants to 
go to college here...

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:17.670
<i>Huh?</i>

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:20.380
<i>I-It's 27 to 13?</i>

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.620
<i>The differential's bad enough, but 27?!</i>

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:25.180
<i>That's only possible if you 
commit a ton of faults.</i>

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.910
<i>What kind of spell has he cast on her?</i>

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.910
<i>That kind of spell...</i>

00:19:34.430 --> 00:19:36.530
<i>As I wait for someone...</i>

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.450
<i>I'm sure she was fast to begin with,</i>

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:42.570
<i>but her game sense is making it easier
for him to bait her into faulting.</i>

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:46.780
<i>I'm so afraid of faulting that I'm not
going all-in on either offense or defense.</i>

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:48.240
<i>My body feels heavy.</i>

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.290
Excuse me.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.710
<i>When I tried to become Suo-san before,</i>

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.170
<i>what did I feel?</i>

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:01.460
<i>He speaks quietly so that others 
will lean closer to hear him.</i>

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:03.490
<i>To learn to live with quiet sounds.</i>

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:05.680
<i>Know exactly where the cards are...</i>

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:06.760
<i>To hold them down...</i>

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:10.650
<i>To become someone who's nothing but ears!</i>

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:16.780
<i>Like the sound of someone 
knocking on my door,</i>

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:16.770
<b>That scared me!</b>

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:15.810
<i>My missed swing made him 
hold down the wrong card!</i>

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:17.560
<i>But I got it! Talk about luck!</i>

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:21.390
<i>If nothing else, with my eyes closed,</i>

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:23.830
<i>I can't be misled by his movements.</i>

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:27.880
<i>I need to be in that mindset 
even without closing my eyes.</i>

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:29.950
<i>Listen closely to the sounds...</i>

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.570
<i>and aim for one point!</i>

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:35.160
<i>I missed again!</i>

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:37.890
<i>I even practiced aiming at a single point!</i>

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:39.420
<i>It clearly wasn't enough!</i>

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:46.970
<i>Okay, once more on this next one.</i>

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.850
<i>Her back shows no sign of resignation...</i>

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.100
Go get turned to mincemeat.

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:57.010
<i>Even if I'm turned to mincemeat, 
I'll never hate karuta!</i>

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:05.030
Thank you very much.

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:08.250
<i>She lost by 14 cards...</i>

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:11.540
<b>Gloom</b>

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:10.550
<i>But she showed some good moves
in the second half.</i>

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:12.530
<i>She's going to get better.</i>

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.230
Oh, sorry.

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:16.990
Sorry.

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:21.520
You're very interesting.

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:22.980
Oh... uh... n-no...

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:26.180
You're pretty, positive, 
and you never lose heart.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:28.380
You have friends, and even a boyfriend.

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:30.140
And you want to be Queen, too?

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:35.690
You can't.
